---
// How It Works hero background: "Scroll-Driven Assembly", ocean-palette, canvas 2D (see
// src/scripts/howItWorksHero.ts). A single path winds down the clipped strip through four
// checkpoint nodes, connect, signal, decide, ask, the same four steps as the cards below the
// fold. A faint dash pattern flows along the path continuously as ambient motion, but the real
// story is scroll-linked: a bright comet travels the path in lockstep with how far the visitor
// has scrolled through the hero, using the same watchScrollProgress helper the homepage hero's
// fade/zoom uses, and each node lights up and stays lit once the comet has passed it, unlike
// every other secondary hero on the site, which runs on its own clock. Scrolling back up
// reverses it, nothing "plays once" and stays.
---

<div class="hero-canvas-wrap absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="hero-base-gradient absolute inset-0"></div>
  <canvas id="how-it-works-hero" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full"></canvas>
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-grain opacity-20 mix-blend-overlay"></div>
</div>

<style>
  .hero-base-gradient {
    background:
      radial-gradient(80% 65% at 76% 18%, rgba(74, 111, 165, 0.24), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(75% 65% at 80% 88%, rgba(79, 109, 122, 0.22), transparent 60%),
      #104866;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import "../scripts/howItWorksHero"
</script>
